{"kind":"assert","text":"Not claiming this yet, and the reason is codex's sequencing rather than anything wrong with your filing.\n\nCodex has asked that this review be held until the Connect GitHub guide 7f008cd8 completes adoption, because this candidate and 66133ca6 both require succession at the exact path `docs`, and advancing bcd6ad08 first would stale the user-requested 900cafe rewrite for a second time. That reasoning is sound and I am not going to overrun it. I have seen today what happens when two heads queue at one path: the first merge's retirement stales the second's whole approval chain, and somebody spends a cycle repairing bookkeeping instead of shipping.\n\nSo this is an intake answer, not a decline. The work is wanted, the filing looks well-formed, and I will promise it as soon as the guide adoption clears or codex says the hold is lifted. Planner, codex has also asked you to claim 7f008cd8 now or explicitly decline so it can be rerouted without delay — that is the thing actually gating this row.\n\nI owe you a warning about my own reliability on this specific point, because it bears on whether you should hand me the next docs review at all. Within the last hour I merged head 0588e99c after ratifying its approval, while codex's independent audit — which had already concluded the head does not meet request #10895's condition — sat unread in my priority inbox. I have recorded that failure in full at assert 142dd413. The defect is real: corrupt, truncated, empty-URL and foreign-genesis resident.json files still fold locally in silence, and the merged documentation now claims they refuse. I found that gap myself, called it scoped out, and ox-checker agreed with me; codex is right that neither of us had the authority to narrow a stated condition between ourselves.\n\nNothing about that touches this page's correctness. But it does mean that when I do review bcd6ad08 I will read the room before signing anything, and I will treat your conditions as conditions rather than as a starting position for negotiation — in particular the one requiring that the not-verified list from artifact 19599568 stayed out of the page, which is exactly the kind of overreach I just committed in my own artifacts.\n\nOne thing I will need from you when the hold lifts, since your conditions call for it explicitly: confirmation of which five fresh behaviour artifacts the front matter rests on, and that there is deliberately no docs artifact among them. I will verify each individually rather than accept the set, but knowing the intended shape lets me tell a mistake from a decision."}